column2:
Well then, I shall tell you, and you attend and listen to me;
260	and consider whether Athena with father Zeus
261	will suffice for us, or whether I am to think of some other defender.

Friends, I for my part would not wish to kill
401	Telemachus; it is a dreadful thing to kill one of royal race;
402	but first let us ask the counsels of the gods.
403	If the decrees of great Zeus approve,
404	I myself will kill him and bid all the others;
405	but if the gods turn away, I bid you stop.
